CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: "Partially realistic but not yet established. The mechanism matches current vLLM-style whole-item encoder scheduling and token/embed-denominated encoder budgets, and the packet's r=0 control plus fixed-T/vary-k design support the mechanism. Gaps: only CPU discrete-event L0; real vLLM/SGLang H100 measurements of ViT intercept/slope, actual chunk budget B, batching interactions, cache-hit rates, and production arrival mixes are missing. The prereg primary stream-p99 prediction is not uniformly supported; realistic small-T Qwen2-VL regimes mainly show worst-iteration single-stall risk."
RATIONALE: "Prompt version v001. This is not integration-only glue: the fixed-per-image ViT cost being invisible to token-budget chunked prefill is a concrete systems mechanism. But it is also not enough for green because closest shipping systems already expose much of the interaction surface: vLLM PR#8425 states multimodal chunked prefill was flaky because multimodal placeholders could not be partially prefilled, and current vLLM code documents encoder-cache scheduling at whole multimodal input granularity with compute/cache budgets measured in encoder embeddings/tokens. I found no OSS evidence that vLLM, SGLang, LMCache, TensorRT-LLM, or FlashInfer already implements the claimed image-count/fixed-overhead-aware scheduler accounting; however, the packet only proves a simulator mechanism with anchored-but-unmeasured r. Required next evidence: real vLLM V1/SGLang run with chunked prefill + encoder cache enabled, fixed total image tokens T while varying image count k, reporting both decode ITL stream-p99 and worst-iteration ITL, plus measured ViT intercept/slope and chunk size."
